WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.193
My name is Kenny and I'm a koala.

2
00:00:03.194 --> 00:00:08.093
I'm native to Australia, which means that I'm originally from there.

3
00:00:08.094 --> 00:00:14.685
I eat, sleep, and live in the eucalyptus forests of Australia.

4
00:00:14.686 --> 00:00:18.572
I eat only the leaves of the eucalyptus trees.

5
00:00:18.573 --> 00:00:22.566
I can eat up to five hundred grams of leaves a night.

6
00:00:22.567 --> 00:00:26.371
At night, you ask? Yes, at night.

7
00:00:26.372 --> 00:00:32.500
I like to eat during the night and sleep during the day. I'm nocturnal.

8
00:00:32.501 --> 00:00:34.856
I don't drink a lot of water.

9
00:00:34.857 --> 00:00:38.799
That's because I get all the water I need from the leaves.

10
00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:44.375
In some of the native Australian languages, koala means "no drink."

11
00:00:44.376 --> 00:00:48.124
That's how we got our name.

12
00:00:48.125 --> 00:00:51.492
I sleep in the branches of the eucalyptus tree.

13
00:00:51.493 --> 00:00:56.009
After I eat, I pick out a nice big branch and sleep.

14
00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:59.012
I usually sleep twenty hours a day.

15
00:00:59.013 --> 00:01:01.138
I sleep a lot, don't I?

16
00:01:01.139 --> 00:01:06.395
The rest of the time, I eat and move around.

17
00:01:06.396 --> 00:01:10.791
I like to live up in the branches of the eucalyptus trees.

18
00:01:10.792 --> 00:01:19.286
I have two thumbs on each paw and long, sharp claws that make it easy for me to climb up and down the tree trunks.

19
00:01:19.287 --> 00:01:23.389
I can also leap from branch to branch.

20
00:01:23.390 --> 00:01:29.141
When I run out of leaves to eat, I climb down and run to another tree.

21
00:01:29.142 --> 00:01:39.459
I don't like to stay on the ground too long because of cars and dangerous predators like the dingo, an Australian wild dog.

22
00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:42.763
I'm a type of animal called a

23
00:01:42.764 --> 00:01:48.814
marsupial. Other marsupials are the kangaroo, the Tasmanian devil, and the

24
00:01:48.815 --> 00:01:57.014
wombat. Marsupials are different from other mammals because, unlike most mammals, the baby is underdeveloped when it's

25
00:01:57.015 --> 00:02:02.001
born. It needs to finish developing in its mother's

26
00:02:02.002 --> 00:02:11.833
pouch. You see, when a baby koala is born, it is very, very small─almost the size of a pink jelly bean.

27
00:02:11.834 --> 00:02:20.084
Although the baby is blind and deaf, it crawls its way into the mommy's pouch.

28
00:02:20.085 --> 00:02:26.058
The baby attaches itself to the mother's nipple to get food to grow big and healthy.

29
00:02:26.059 --> 00:02:29.290
A baby marsupial is called a joey.

30
00:02:29.291 --> 00:02:33.265
So, baby kangaroos are also called joeys.

31
00:02:33.266 --> 00:02:37.560
First, the joey develops eyes, ears, and fur.

32
00:02:37.561 --> 00:02:45.210
At about five months, the joey's eyes open and it's able to peer out of the pouch.

33
00:02:45.211 --> 00:02:51.624
When it is six months old, the joey gets too big for the pouch and can't fit inside.

34
00:02:51.625 --> 00:02:57.973
When that happens, the joey rides on the back of its mother.

35
00:02:57.974 --> 00:03:04.496
A joey leaves its mother when it becomes one year old, or when it gets a little brother or sister.

36
00:03:04.497 --> 00:03:09.281
In my case, I enjoyed staying with my mommy until I was one.

37
00:03:09.282 --> 00:03:14.609
But I was also very excited to go off on my own.

38
00:03:14.610 --> 00:03:16.834
I like to live by myself.

39
00:03:16.835 --> 00:03:23.503
I'm territorial, which means that I don't like other koalas coming too close to where I live.

40
00:03:23.504 --> 00:03:30.973
But if you're nice, you can visit me anytime.

